# What this repository is, and is not.
#
# It holds the CODE and the SMALL RELEASED ARTEFACTS of the cross-dataset weld
# generalization study: scripts, the frozen split lists, the hash manifests
# that pin them, the exact lineage, and the analysis tables and figures.
#
# It deliberately holds NO IMAGES and NO CHECKPOINTS. Roughly 38 GB of this
# working tree is image data, trained weights and pulled results. Three reasons
# to keep all of it out:
#
#   1. Licensing. The five original dataset folders belong to their authors.
#      The data availability statement promises that originals are obtained
#      from the cited sources, not redistributed by us. GDXray in particular is
#      research and educational use only with no redistribution.
#   2. Reproducibility does not need them. The project log "Split reproducibility"
#      establishes that the released artefact is the frozen split FILES and
#      their sha256 hashes, not a re-run of the solver. Those files are
#      tracked. Anyone can verify a rebuilt tree against them.
#   3. Size. A git history is not a backup system for 21 GB of checkpoints.
#
# The rule below is deny-by-default for anything bulky, then re-include the
# specific small artefacts. Adding a new big directory therefore fails safe.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv-weld/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ------------------------------------------------- original third-party data
# Not ours to redistribute. Obtain from the sources cited in the project log.
/Weld Surface Defect Detection.v1i.yolov8/
/Weld Surface Defect Detection.v2i.yolov8/
/Welding Defect, Object Detection_kaggle/
/Visual Welding Defect.v1i.yolov8/
/welding defect 2class.v1i.yolov8/
/LoHi-WELD weld-dataset/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ derived trees
# lohi_weld_yolo/ is a conversion staging area, rebuilt by lohi_to_yolo.py.
# clean/ is the SUPERSEDED 3 September tree and must not be used at all.
/lohi_weld_yolo/
/clean/

# --------------------------------------------------- the audited clean tree
# Exclude the images, keep the artefacts that define the partition. The
# re-includes below are what make the splits verifiable without the pixels.
/clean_candidate/*
!/clean_candidate/splits/
!/clean_candidate/split_hashes.json
!/clean_candidate/manifest.csv
!/clean_candidate/before_after.md
!/clean_candidate/*.json
!/clean_candidate/*.md

# Arm datasets are views of the frozen splits, materialised by
# grid/arms/build_arm_datasets.py. Their hash manifest is tracked instead.
/clean_candidate/lohi_high/
/clean_candidate/lohi_low/
/clean_candidate/pool_no_*/

# ------------------------------------------------------ weights and results
# Checkpoints are pinned by sha256 in models/pretrained/manifest.json, which IS
# tracked. The .pt files themselves are downloads.
/models/pretrained/*.pt
/models/pretrained/*.pth
/weights/
/runs/
/runs_arms/
/results/
/results_arms/

# Pulled cluster results. The analysis output is re-included below because the
# tables and figures are manuscript artefacts.
/grid_results/*
/grid_results_arms/*
!/grid_results/analysis/
!/grid_results_arms/analysis/
# The thin-class bootstrap cache is re-included too. build_results_section.py
# reads its key to check the draw count the captions quote, so a clone
# without it cannot build the manuscript. It is keyed by resample count and
# seed and names no path, so it is the same in every checkout.
!/grid_results/bootstrap_cache.json

# Journal submission folders, written by build_results_section.py --clean.
# The manuscript, highlights, figure PDFs and EPS files and the checklist are
# tracked as the uploads. The 1000 dpi PNGs are only what the Word file
# embeds, and the fallback journal's draft is a working file.
/submission/*/embed/
/submission/*/Manuscript_draft.docx

# grid/dirty/ is a 179 MB symlink farm of the ORIGINAL shipped splits, rebuilt
# by grid/make_dirty_yaml.py. Its content hashes are recorded in the cell
# provenance, so the farm itself is disposable.
/grid/dirty/

# grid/fixtures/per_class_nms_cache.json is not tracked, unlike its two
# siblings there. Those are keyed by resample count and seed, which are the
# same in every checkout, so a fixture run leaves them unchanged. This one is
# keyed by the absolute path of the results directory, so a tracked copy would
# name one checkout and mismatch in every other. Since 25 September 2026 no
# fixture run writes it. The fixtures ship no raw__*.npz archives, and
# per_class_nms.py writes no cache when there is nothing to correct. The rule
# stays so that a copy left by an earlier run is never committed.
/grid/fixtures/per_class_nms_cache.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- audit
# The pair montages are 43 MB of rendered JPEGs and hashes.json is 9.4 MB of
# perceptual hashes, both regenerable. The VERDICTS are the evidence, and
# sampled_pairs.csv is small, so it stays.
/audit_out/pairs/*.jpg
/audit_out/pairs/*.png
/audit_out/hashes.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- logs
*.log
/grid_results_arms_watch.log
/grid_results/logs/
/grid_results_arms/logs/
/grid_results_arms/extracted/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ scratch
/tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*~
.DS_Store

# Manuscript builds. build_results_section.py writes these, so they are
# outputs rather than sources.
/Weld_Transfer_Results_Section.docx
/Weld_Transfer_Results_Section_clean.docx
/submission/

# Exploratory matched-step control, the project log 6a-xi. Checkpoints, per-cell
# evaluation records and raw predictions are NOT tracked, exactly as for the
# main grid and the arms: 9b keeps code, split lists and analysis outputs in
# the repository and leaves the heavy artefacts out.
#
# The first version of this block ended `!/grid_results_msc/*/`, which
# re-included every subdirectory and would have committed 55 MB of raw npz.
# Only the two small report artefacts are tracked.
/runs_msc/
/grid_results_msc/*
!/grid_results_msc/matched_step_control.md
!/grid_results_msc/matched_step_control.csv
